{"name":"Night Thistle","hex":"#6b7ba7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"},{"term":"thistle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several perennial composite plants, especially of genera Cirsium, Carduus, Cynara, or Onopordum, having prickly leaves and showy flower heads with prickly bracts.","This plant seen as the national emblem of Scotland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thistle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Thistle","blocks":[{"text":"Thistle is the popular name of a group of flowering plants characterised by leaves with sharp spikes on the margins, mostly in the family Asteraceae. Prickles can also occur all over the plant – on the stem, and on the flat parts of the leaves. These prickles protect the plant from herbivores. Typically, an involucre with a clasping shape, similar to a cup or urn, subtends each of a thistle's flower heads. The typically feathery pappus of a ripe thistle flower is known as thistle-down."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Carduus_Nutans_in_the_Carpathian_Mountains.jpg/330px-Carduus_Nutans_in_the_Carpathian_Mountains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thistle","wikidata":"Q538906"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"},{"title":"Shades of purple","blocks":[{"text":"There are numerous variations of the color purple, a sampling of which is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Shades_of_Purple.svg/330px-Shades_of_Purple.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_purple","wikidata":"Q7460344"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png/500px-Owl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Variable spellings of night in a Middle English poem:\n\nÞu sittest a dai & fliȝst a niȝt (top)\nÞu sittest a day and flyhst a niht (bottom)\n'You sit by day and fly by night'\n\n","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOwl_and_the_Nightingale_comparison.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/1280px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png/500px-Earth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Day and night during the winter solstice in the northern hemisphere","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth-lighting-winter-solstice_EN.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/500px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/1280px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG/500px-Nile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The drainage basin of the Nile River and delta at night","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANile_River_Delta_at_Night.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/MarsSunset.jpg/500px-MarsSunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org